  "question": {
    "text": "Three particles, each of mass $m$ gram, are situated at the vertices of an equilateral triangle $A B C$ of side $\\ell \\mathrm{~cm}$ (as shown in the figure). The moment of inertia of the system about a line $A X$ perpendicular to $A B$ and in the plane of $A B C$, in gram $-\\mathrm{cm}^2$ units will be\r\n\r\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0005_b3c4b73fb43d.png\">"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{2} m l^{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{4} m l^{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 m l^{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{4} m l^{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0005_5828936a0546.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{AX}}=\\mathrm{m}(\\mathrm{AB})^{2}+\\mathrm{m}(\\mathrm{OC})^{2}=\\mathrm{m} l^{2}+\\mathrm{m}\\left(l \\cos 60^{\\circ}\\right)^{2}=m l^{2}+\\frac{\\mathrm{m} l^{2}}{4}=\\frac{5}{4} \\mathrm{~m} l^{2}$"
  }
}